  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Anduril Industries obligated $804M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Anduril Industries received 68 awards this fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $11.8M, and obligations were up 81.7% year over year. Anduril Industries has grown from $52.5M in FY21, to $211M in FY22, $233M in FY23, $645M in FY24, and $442M in FY25, before reaching $804M in FY26. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $422M, followed by Department of Defense at $342M and Department of Energy at $40M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market by NAICS at $518M, with Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing next at $222M. Anduril Industries also shows activity in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $40.8M and in Aircraft Manufacturing at $20.1M. The fiscal totals for the current year are partial and reflect contract obligations rather than full contract values where noted.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Anduril Industries' federal business trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Anduril Industries obligated $52.5M in FY21 and rose to $211M in FY22, $233M in FY23, $645M in FY24, $442M in FY25, and $804M in FY26. Anduril Industries obligations were up 81.7% year over year for FY2026 to date, reflecting the larger award flow and higher average award size of $11.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets drive Anduril Industries' federal revenue?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security obligated $422M and Department of Defense obligated $342M in FY2026 to date, with Department of Energy obligating $40M. Computer Systems Design Services leads the markets at $518M, followed by Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $222M."
      }
    ]
  },
